Yes. Forgetting can hide the wound; forgiveness changes your relationship to it.

You don’t have to erase what happened, excuse every choice, or pretend it didn’t matter. Self-forgiveness is more like: tell the truth, accept that the past is fixed, repair what can still be repaired, learn the lesson, and stop using the lesson as a weapon against yourself.

And loving yourself doesn’t require believing every past version of you was right. It means refusing to make your worth contingent on never having failed.

Remember enough to learn. Forgive enough to live. Love yourself enough to keep becoming.